---
import ProseLayout from '@/layouts/ProseLayout.astro';

// The site's actual thesis, stated in the copy below ("The editorial unit
// here is a chain") - worth showing as a real chain, not just saying so in
// prose. The one deliberate bit of boldness on this page; everything else
// here stays as plain paragraphs.
const chain = [
  { label: 'Research claim', detail: 'What the literature or docs say, and its limitations' },
  { label: 'Runtime invariant', detail: 'The rule that actually gets violated in production' },
  { label: 'Operational evidence', detail: 'Traces, costs, failures, recovery behavior' },
  { label: 'Reproducible artifact', detail: 'What a reader can run or inspect themselves' },
];
---

<ProseLayout
  eyebrow="About"
  title="What Runtime Signals is for"
  description="Runtime Signals connects research claims, runtime invariants, operational evidence, and reproducible artifacts."
  canonicalPath="/about"
  traceSeed={3}
>
  <p>
    Runtime Signals is not an AI news site. It publishes system-level analysis of evaluation,
    reliability, recovery, orchestration, state, memory, tool security, distributed execution,
    observability, and failure analysis for AI agents running in production.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most coverage of agent systems is either research summary or product announcement. Neither
    connects the four layers that actually determine whether a system holds up under load:
  </p>

  <ol class="chain" aria-label="The four layers every piece connects, in order">
    {
      chain.map((link, i) => (
        <li>
          <span class="chain__index" aria-hidden="true">
            {i + 1}
          </span>
          <div class="chain__content">
            <span class="chain__label">{link.label}</span>
            <span class="chain__detail">{link.detail}</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p>
    The editorial unit here is a chain: a real failure mechanism, the invariant it violates, and the
    engineering practice that holds under load. That's narrower than general AI commentary, and it's
    the whole point.
  </p>
  <h2>What we commit to</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>No unreviewed AI-generated articles are published.</li>
    <li>
      Every consequential factual claim has a source record or is explicitly marked inference or
      opinion.
    </li>
    <li>
      Source records preserve URL, publisher, publication date, access date, evidence type, and what
      the source supports.
    </li>
    <li>Articles state limitations and workload or configuration boundaries.</li>
    <li>A human approves publication, meaningful updates, corrections, and syndicated versions.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    See <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> for how claims are labeled and sourced, and <a
      href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a
    > for the review process itself.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>

<style>
  .chain {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .chain li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  /* The connecting line: a hairline running through each index mark's
     center, continuous from the first link to the last - the literal "chain"
     the copy names. */
  .chain li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.85rem;
    top: 2.2rem;
    bottom: -0.5rem;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--hairline);
  }

  .chain__index {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--signal);
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    background: var(--paper);
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .chain__content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15em;
    padding-top: 0.15em;
  }

  .chain__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .chain__detail {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
